     "A 3D array mapping each brick to its selected LOD level $k$.",
     "*   **Texture Dimensions:** Due to OpenGL power-of-two restrictions, textures are expanded to the next power of two.",
     "Let $P(L)$ be the smallest power of two $\\ge L$.",
     "*   **Merged Textures:** To save memory, adjacent bricks at coarser levels share textures.",
     "*   **Time Complexity:** LOD selection is $O(B)$ where $B$ is the number of bricks.",
     "Hierarchy construction is $O(V)$ where $V$ is the total voxel count.",
     "Rendering is $O(P \\cdot S)$ where $P$ is pixels and $S$ is samples, but $S$ is reduced by LOD.",
     "*   **Memory Complexity:** Texture memory usage is significantly reduced."
    ]
   }
  }
